# clang-tidy over Phazite's own code (src/ and tests/, never external/): a small set of checks for real bugs, each passing
# today, every finding an error. tools/clang-tidy.sh runs them over a build's compile_commands.json; CI's Clang job does
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml). A check joins the list once its findings are fixed; one that finds only false alarms here
# stays off. What each catches:
# - bugprone-use-after-move: an object read after std::move took its contents.
# - bugprone-dangling-handle: a std::string_view or std::span left pointing into a temporary.
# - bugprone-unused-raii: a lock, a gesture or another scoped object made and destroyed at once (a name forgotten).
# - bugprone-undelegated-constructor, bugprone-copy-constructor-init: a constructor that builds a temporary of its own class,
#   or a copy that leaves its base unset.
# - bugprone-move-forwarding-reference, bugprone-forwarding-reference-overload: std::move on a forwarding reference, and a
#   perfect-forwarding constructor that hides the copy and move ones.
# - bugprone-string-constructor, bugprone-string-literal-with-embedded-nul, bugprone-suspicious-string-compare,
#   bugprone-misplaced-operator-in-strlen-in-alloc: strings made or compared wrongly.
# - bugprone-suspicious-memset-usage, bugprone-undefined-memory-manipulation, bugprone-sizeof-container: memory written
#   or measured wrongly.
# - bugprone-unhandled-self-assignment, bugprone-virtual-near-miss, bugprone-parent-virtual-call: classes that misbehave
#   when assigned to themselves, or override a function they don't.
# - bugprone-throw-keyword-missing, bugprone-terminating-continue, bugprone-suspicious-semicolon, bugprone-fold-init-type,
#   bugprone-bool-pointer-implicit-conversion, bugprone-inaccurate-erase, bugprone-infinite-loop: slips of the pen.
# - clang-analyzer-core.*, clang-analyzer-cplusplus.*: Clang's static analyzer, path by path: undefined values, memory
#   leaked, freed twice or used after it is freed, objects used after a move. But for seven of its checks, which found only
#   what an invariant the analyzer can't see rules out (2026-11-14): a ValueTree found in the song only when there is a
#   song (NonNullParamChecker, 11 times); a helper's instance there whenever its channel opened (CallAndMessage); a voice
#   to take whenever all are playing (UndefReturn, NullDereference); a lambda's moved std::function (StackAddressEscape);
#   a sample rate under 100 Hz (UndefinedBinaryOperatorResult); a component's row height (DivideZero).
#   tests/.clang-tidy turns its memory checks off for the tests, whose doctest macros trip them in doctest's own code.
# Off: bugprone-incorrect-roundings, whose one finding, (int) (x + 0.5f) for a value never negative, is right; and
# bugprone-swapped-arguments, whose one finding (a test's int and double, in the order its function takes them) is too.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-use-after-move,
  bugprone-dangling-handle,
  bugprone-unused-raii,
  bugprone-undelegated-constructor,
  bugprone-copy-constructor-init,
  bugprone-move-forwarding-reference,
  bugprone-forwarding-reference-overload,
  bugprone-string-constructor,
  bugprone-string-literal-with-embedded-nul,
  bugprone-suspicious-string-compare,
  bugprone-misplaced-operator-in-strlen-in-alloc,
  bugprone-suspicious-memset-usage,
  bugprone-undefined-memory-manipulation,
  bugprone-sizeof-container,
  bugprone-unhandled-self-assignment,
  bugprone-virtual-near-miss,
  bugprone-parent-virtual-call,
  bugprone-throw-keyword-missing,
  bugprone-terminating-continue,
  bugprone-suspicious-semicolon,
  bugprone-fold-init-type,
  bugprone-bool-pointer-implicit-conversion,
  bugprone-inaccurate-erase,
  bugprone-infinite-loop,
  clang-analyzer-core.*,
  -clang-analyzer-core.NonNullParamChecker,
  -clang-analyzer-core.CallAndMessage,
  -clang-analyzer-core.uninitialized.UndefReturn,
  -clang-analyzer-core.StackAddressEscape,
  -clang-analyzer-core.UndefinedBinaryOperatorResult,
  -clang-analyzer-core.DivideZero,
  -clang-analyzer-core.NullDereference,
  clang-analyzer-cplusplus.*
WarningsAsErrors: "*"
# Findings in Phazite's own headers too; JUCE's, doctest's and the other submodules' are theirs.
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*[/\\](src|tests)[/\\].*'
